WEBVTT

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.240
Project Mew’s ultimate goal,
their search for Mew, has finally begun.

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.990
However,
with all of their devices unusable,

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:14.160
the ascent of Table Mountain
was extremely difficult.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:19.750
On top of that,
an accident caused the team to split in two,

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.380
and Groudon appeared
before Tsurugi and Shigeru...

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:29.010
...as Kaiogre appeared
before Go, Tokio, and Asahi.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:33.680
Will they be able to escape this predicament
and encounter Mew?

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:23.620
The Legendary Pokémon that raises the lands,
said to be the land incarnate...

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:25.380
Groudon!

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:34.550
The Legendary Pokémon that creates seas
out of heavy rainfall, said to be the sea incarnate...

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:36.300
Kaiogre!

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.760
What an incredibly
rare encounter...

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:41.430
Get back!

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.520
Manyula! Lightning Speed!

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:54.900
Ice Shard!

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:02.160
That should be super effective
against Ground types.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:03.250
Next attack’s coming!

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:09.000
Evil Pulse!

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:14.300
Manyula!

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:21.930
Precipice Blades?!

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:23.770
Over here!

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:24.890
Groudon!

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:32.320
<i>I’m</i> your opponent!

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:34.690
You two...

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:49.710
Are you okay?

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:50.790
Yeah.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:51.710
Let’s tail it.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:54.840
Something’s weird
about that Groudon.

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:01.970
It’s dangerous,
so you hide back here.

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:06.100
Dodge, Marilluri!

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:11.060
Hydro Pump!

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:16.740
Marilluri!

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:21.200
No way...
Is that Origin Pulse?!

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.080
Kaiogre!

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:25.950
Over here!

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:27.080
Go...

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:33.880
Over here! Kaiogre!

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:35.550
Ms. Asahi,
get away while you can!

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:36.210
Look out!

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:48.060
Sarunori!

00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:58.400
Sarunori!

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:12.500
Huh...?

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:13.750
Go, Tokio.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:16.300
We’re following that Kaiogre.
Stay close.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:17.420
Yes, ma’am!

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:24.640
Thank you, Sarunori.

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:29.430
It made me happy to see you
doing your best to save me.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:31.810
That Wood Hammer
was really cool!

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:53.920
What?

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:55.920
Kaiogre?!

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:58.550
Ms. Asahi’s there, too.

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:00.670
That voice...

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:02.260
Shigeru?

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:03.760
Look out!

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:16.150
Mew!

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:32.500
Huh?

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:33.660
What?

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:56.270
What is this?

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:24.550
Huh...? Where am I?

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:38.690
Space?

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:44.360
I’m... flying?

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:47.990
What’s that?

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:03.300
Wh-What the—?!

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:29.780
Mew!

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:34.950
Wait!

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:43.210
That’s...
the island where we were...

00:08:55.850 --> 00:08:57.060
What was that?!

00:08:57.060 --> 00:09:00.060
Space... The sea... The sky...

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:02.310
Rekkuuza... and Mew...

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:04.020
We all had the same dream?

00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:06.400
A supernova...

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:09.240
Stars and galaxies being born...

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:13.240
Is this rock a crystallization
of the memories of the universe?

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:20.290
Huh?! Did I... do that?

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:32.930
It disappeared again...

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:47.440
Rampard! Torideps!

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:52.700
Gachigoras... Even Armaldo...

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:59.750
The Pokémon are upset
that the light from the rocks faded?

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:02.040
This is Hodaka!
Can you hear me?!

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:04.580
Yes, we hear you.

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:05.750
The transmitter!

00:10:06.170 --> 00:10:07.210
Mine’s back, too!

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:08.130
And mine!

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:11.130
We can even use
our Monster Balls!

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:14.300
Professor,
our devices are all working again.

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:17.560
Is that right?
That’s good news.

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:21.560
The sensor is responding!

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:30.530
Mew!

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:11.280
Wulaosu! Evil Pulse!

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:18.070
Wulaosu! Focus Blast!

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:30.670
Here it comes!

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:34.130
Infight!

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:49.810
Return!

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:51.860
Manyula!

00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:52.820
Marilluri!

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:55.190
Come out, Kamex!

00:11:58.450 --> 00:12:00.740
Shigeru,
what are you trying to do?

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:03.330
There’s no way to calm Mew down
but to battle it!

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:05.870
But it’s probably
just playing around!

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:11.460
I’ll lend you guys support!

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:20.720
Manyula! Evil Pulse!

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:22.640
Marilluri! Ice Beam!

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:24.810
Kamex! Hydro Pump!

00:12:24.810 --> 00:12:26.560
Aceburn! Pyro Ball!

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:37.950
Sirknight! Light Screen!

00:12:49.670 --> 00:12:51.330
What power...!

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:02.640
I knew this battle was hopeless!

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:03.220
Go!

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:05.350
Calm down, Mew!

00:13:10.690 --> 00:13:12.440
Marilluri! Hydro Pump!

00:13:12.440 --> 00:13:13.940
Manyula! Ice Shard!

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:16.860
Kamex! Water Pulse!

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:22.530
Sirknight! Light Screen!

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:40.300
R-Return!

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:43.300
Please!
You have to calm down!

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:48.600
I’ve longed to see you again,
but not like this!

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:50.680
Come out, Donkarasu!

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:55.230
You’re still going?

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:56.570
I told you...

00:13:56.570 --> 00:13:59.030
Mew can be
an angel or a demon!

00:13:59.030 --> 00:14:03.110
But like Go said,
it could just be playing around.

00:14:08.290 --> 00:14:11.960
If we let it keep rampaging,
the other Pokémon will be in danger.

00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:13.540
We have to stop Mew.

00:14:14.210 --> 00:14:15.920
But how?

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:18.420
For crying out loud...

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:52.910
Satoshi...

00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:00.340
Yeah... I...

00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:02.920
...won’t give up, either!

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:06.300
Mew!

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:09.970
You may not remember me,

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:11.810
but we’ve met before!

00:15:14.730 --> 00:15:18.610
Ever since,
I’ve been interested in you,

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:20.820
wondering how I might
get to see you again.

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:23.320
I did so much research.

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:31.370
You’re the reason
I set out into the world!

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:35.540
And the reason I met Satoshi,

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:37.460
the reason I became
a research fellow,

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:40.290
the reason I’ve traveled
to all sorts of regions,

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:42.710
the reason I’ve learned about
all sorts of Pokémon...

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:47.720
Everything I am today
is because of you!

00:15:48.140 --> 00:15:49.300
It’s using Destroyer Beam?!

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:50.180
Get back!

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:54.930
So there’s something I’ve wanted to tell you
if we ever met again!

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:58.310
Thank you!

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:07.950
Mew...

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:45.000
Does this mean it’s...
game over?

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:50.170
Thank you, Mew.

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:54.010
I promise
I’ll come see you again.

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:56.930
That future lies in...

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:14.490
In my hands!

00:18:28.550 --> 00:18:30.670
Wet season has arrived.

00:18:31.010 --> 00:18:34.180
Unfortunately,
our search ends here.

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:37.180
But we’ve gained much from it.

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:39.930
We successfully
managed to encounter Mew.

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:45.900
The supernova and galaxies
we saw forming... What was that?

00:18:45.900 --> 00:18:51.190
Could the origins of space and the stars
be closely linked to the origins of Pokémon?

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:52.610
There could indeed.

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:54.780
When I asked myself
the same thing...

00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:57.820
I couldn’t help but imagine
Mew laughing.

00:18:58.280 --> 00:18:59.620
I see.

00:18:59.620 --> 00:19:02.080
So it may have just been
teasing us humans,

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:05.710
showing us nothing more
than an illusion.

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:07.210
Yes.

00:19:07.210 --> 00:19:11.090
So only it
really knows for sure.

00:19:11.090 --> 00:19:14.550
The more we try and explain
the mysteries of Mew,

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:17.220
the more mysterious they become.

00:19:17.640 --> 00:19:19.550
It truly is a riddle.

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:23.350
Which is why it’s such a fascinating
Pokémon to research.

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:30.440
With this, the Chasers
are temporarily disbanded.

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:33.860
I’ll recruit again
when our next project begins,

00:19:34.240 --> 00:19:37.030
but you’d be welcome
to stay on as Chasers.

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:41.990
Tsurugi and Asahi
have already decided to stay on.

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:43.500
What about you?

00:19:44.040 --> 00:19:45.370
I’m not sure yet...

00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:46.580
Nor me.

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:48.630
I’ll think it over carefully.

00:19:49.670 --> 00:19:52.380
Yes, please do.
There is no rush.

00:19:52.380 --> 00:19:53.760
And if you do stay on,

00:19:54.300 --> 00:19:58.140
I’ll be gentle with your training,
so look forward to that.

00:20:00.390 --> 00:20:08.100
I believe your pure-hearted wishes to meet Mew
are the reason it showed itself to us.

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:10.690
Thank you very much
for participating.

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:14.610
Tsurugi, won’t you
say something, too?

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:26.960
We didn’t make a bad team.

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:28.540
Thanks.

00:20:30.630 --> 00:20:32.090
Likewise...

00:20:32.090 --> 00:20:34.050
<i>Thank you very much!</i>

00:20:38.430 --> 00:20:40.550
Well, I’ll be off.

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:41.970
Give my regards to Satoshi.

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:43.220
Sure.

00:20:43.220 --> 00:20:45.850
I’m glad I met you, Shigeru.

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:50.350
So am I.

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:57.190
Tokio.

00:20:58.530 --> 00:21:02.990
Track down all the Psychic types
and reach Celebi, okay?

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:04.490
Yeah!

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:05.990
You do your best too, Go!

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:08.120
<i>That future lies...</i>

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:10.750
<i>...in our hands!</i>

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:16.590
Project Mew ends,

00:21:16.590 --> 00:21:20.970
and Go, Tokio, and Shigeru
each go their separate ways.

00:21:21.720 --> 00:21:25.510
What sort of future
lies ahead of them?

00:21:34.190 --> 00:21:37.070
Calling! Calling!

00:21:37.070 --> 00:21:38.780
Hello? Go?

00:21:38.780 --> 00:21:41.150
Satoshi! How’d it go?

00:21:41.530 --> 00:21:43.410
Your finals match with
Mr. Dande!

00:23:07.120 --> 00:23:09.580
Now, off to the next adventure!

00:23:09.580 --> 00:23:10.870
Go!

00:23:11.660 --> 00:23:14.710
I’d like to...
set off on a journey.

00:23:14.710 --> 00:23:16.630
Have you told Satoshi?

00:23:16.630 --> 00:23:19.040
Oh, he’d tell me to go for it.

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:20.960
I know what he’s like.

00:23:20.960 --> 00:23:21.630
And...

00:23:21.630 --> 00:23:23.340
Sorry I’m late!

00:23:23.970 --> 00:23:25.630
Huh? Something wrong?

00:23:25.630 --> 00:23:27.050
No, um...

00:23:27.470 --> 00:23:28.140
I...

00:23:29.010 --> 00:23:30.930
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:30.930 --> 00:23:33.850
Pokémon!
I’m Glad I Met You!

00:23:36.020 --> 00:23:36.770
Here we go!

00:23:36.770 --> 00:23:38.900
Championing the evils of truth and love!

00:23:38.900 --> 00:23:40.570
Team Rocket Explorers!

00:23:41.400 --> 00:23:44.820
Following an order
to catch new Pokémon...

00:23:44.820 --> 00:23:47.700
...we made our first visit
to the Paldea Region.

00:23:47.700 --> 00:23:50.200
Oh, meow?
There’s one, meow!

00:23:50.580 --> 00:23:52.080
I think that one’s...

00:23:52.080 --> 00:23:54.950
The Fire Croc Pokémon,
Hogator.

00:23:55.330 --> 00:24:00.960
It’s laid-back and does things at its own pace,
but it’ll sprint toward any food it finds with a glint in its eye.

00:24:00.960 --> 00:24:03.130
That sounds a lot like Nyarth.

00:24:03.130 --> 00:24:05.090
Or a lot like Musashi, meow.

00:24:05.090 --> 00:24:06.760
Let’s catch it quick!

00:24:06.760 --> 00:24:07.590
Yeah!

00:24:07.590 --> 00:24:09.050
Musashi, is that...?

00:24:09.050 --> 00:24:10.550
Huh? Oh! An Oran Berry...

00:24:18.730 --> 00:24:21.360
<i>What an awful feeling!</i>

00:24:24.860 --> 00:24:26.070
Today’s roundup!

00:24:26.070 --> 00:24:27.070
Hogator is...

00:24:27.070 --> 00:24:28.490
...a glutton!
